Theorem~\ref{thm:waveguide_to_pa_channel} shows that each row of
$\bm H^{(\mathrm{W}\to\mathrm{P})}$
is formed by the ordered cascade of coupled propagation and the
residual-field factors introduced by all preceding PAs.
The current PA then extracts the field amplitude
$\sin(\kappa\tau_q)$ from its hosting waveguide.
Together with the PA-to-agent channel in
\eqref{eq:pa_user_channel_matrix}, the waveguide-to-PA
channel in \eqref{eq:waveguide_to_pa_channel} completes
the effective end-to-end channel $\bm H$ in
\eqref{eq:end_to_end}.

\section{Coupling-Aware Rate Upper Bounds}\label{sec:IV}

\begin{figure*}[!t]
\normalsize
