\subsection{Algorithm Performance}
We first evaluate the convergence behavior of the proposed
WMMSE-SCA and PDD algorithms, followed by a comparison of
their achievable rates under different transmit power levels.
\subsubsection{Convergence Behavior}
Fig.~\ref{fig:convergence} compares the sum-rate
convergence of WMMSE-SCA and PDD under different
initial penalty parameters $\rho_0$.
The main observations are as follows.
\begin{itemize}
 \item \textit{Convergence of WMMSE-SCA:}
 WMMSE-SCA exhibits rapid initial improvement,
 reaching approximately 50~bps/Hz within
 15 iterations, followed by gradual convergence
 toward 58~bps/Hz.
 \item \textit{Impact of the initial penalty parameter:}
 PDD convergence is sensitive to $\rho_0$.
 With $\rho_0=0.1$, PDD converges fastest,
 approaching 58~bps/Hz within 35 iterations.
 Larger values of $\rho_0$ lead to slower
 convergence and slightly lower final rates,
 as highlighted by the inset.
 \item \textit{Comparison of the proposed algorithms:}
 WMMSE-SCA achieves faster initial convergence,
 while PDD with $\rho_0=0.1$ reaches a
 comparable final rate with fewer iterations.
 Overall, both algorithms achieve similar
 sum-rate performance, although appropriate
 penalty initialization is important for PDD.
\end{itemize}
\subsubsection{Achievable Rate}
