\subsection{Inference Latency Analysis}
The primary motivation of the proposed framework is the reduction of online beamforming latency. The performance of each method at 10dB SNR and $T_{B}=10$ms is summarized in Table.\ref{tab:table1} for LFM signals. The average prediction time required to generate beamforming weights for each method is provided in this table. The benchmark approaches require both DoA estimation and beamformer computation, resulting in prediction times between $3.3\times10^{-3}$ s and $3.9\times10^{-3}$s. In contrast, BFDNN directly generates beamforming weights through a single forward pass of the neural network and requires only $1.313\times10^{-4}$s. The measured results correspond to a latency reduction of approximately 25-30 times, relative to the benchmark methods on the evaluated platform.
Table~\ref{tab:table1} shows that the proposed BFDNN achieves competitive DoA RMSE and higher ESE at the lowest inference latency among all compared methods. These results indicate that direct covariance-to-beamformer learning  maintains competitive sensing accuracy and favorable communication performance in the considered ISAC scenario, demonstrating the efficiency of the proposed method.
