 \subfloat[Outer AO framework. \label{fig:conv_ao}]{
 \includegraphics[width=0.24\textwidth]{Fig/conv_AO}}
 \caption{Convergence behavior of the proposed framework.}
 \label{fig:algorithm_convergence}
\end{figure*}
Fig.~\ref{fig:algorithm_convergence} verifies the convergence reliability of the proposed framework.  Fig.~\ref{fig:conv_f} plots the successive change of $|\lambda_{\rm D}^{(i+1)}-\lambda_{\rm D}^{(i)}|/W$, which rapidly vanishes as $(\mathbf F_{\rm BB}, \mathbf F_{\rm RF})$-subproblem approaches its stationary solution. Fig.~\ref{fig:conv_r} shows a similar decay in $|\eta_{\rm R}^{(q+1)}-\eta_{\rm R}^{(q)}|/W$, confirming stable convergence of the $\mathbf R$-subproblem. For $\mathbf Z$-subproblem, the upper-panel of Fig.~\ref{fig:conv_z} reports the number of antenna-state changes during each complete sweep over $N$ MPRAs ($(p-1)N\sim pN$). The lower panel shows the corresponding sweep-wise variation in the normalized EE. Specifically, both \(\sum_{i=(q-1)N+1}^{qN} b_{\rm pat}^{[i]}\) and \(\lvert\eta_{\rm EE}^{[qN]}-\eta_{\rm EE}^{[(q-1)N]}\rvert/W\) progressively approach zero, indicating that the cyclic pattern search reaches a coordinate-wise stationary point. Finally, Fig.~\ref{fig:conv_ao} also shows that $|\eta_{\rm EE}^{(t)}-\eta_{\rm EE}^{(t-1)}|/W$ decreases to zero within only a few iterations. Overall, the stable convergence behavior clearly demonstrates the reliability.
